00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:23.220
are there's two types of b12 there's a
pseudo b12 and there's like real b12 so

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:29.189
pseudo means it's like a fake b12 and
it's called a b12 analogue what that

00:00:29.189 --> 00:00:36.360
means it's similar in chemistry but not
very similar in function so if an algae

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:42.870
has larger amounts of pseudo b12 or b12
analogue that is going to block that

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:47.160
small bit of trace real b12 that's in
there and you're going to end up with

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:53.100
the deficiency so unless you're
consuming extra b12 from a supplement or

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:58.800
something I do not recommend trying to
get your b12 from nori or spirulina on

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:04.350
the other hand chlorella has much
greater amounts of actual real b12 and

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:09.150
very trace amounts of the pseudo
analogue b12 so then the question is how

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:13.350
